    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct chlorprothixene absolute oral bioavailability record is present.",
    "No IV-comparison or matched oral/reference exposure data for the query molecule.",
    "No formulation, prandial state, or dose condition is specified for the query.",
    "First-pass metabolism and solubility for chlorprothixene are not directly measured in the supplied records.",
    "L3 midazolam exposure records are not applicable to the query and provide no threshold-relevant F information."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Transferable human records for lipophilic basic CNS drugs (alprazolam 92%, trazodone 63–91%, triazolam 36–55%) all support F≥20%, and the query's physicochemical profile (low MW, low TPSA, basic amine, logD 3.55) favors absorption. No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence indicates F<20%; the only low F record is a rat-specific alprazolam value with low transferability. L3 midazolam AUC/Cmax records are for a different molecule and do not alter the decision. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

